      "claim": "9-AC, a lactone-containing molecule, has oral bioavailability of about 49% (range 27–49%) in patients, supporting that lactone-containing polar molecules can exceed 20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C10", "C21"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The low-F records (omadacycline 0.6% fed high-fat; CGP 43371 9%) come from aromatic/basic or food-affected molecules and are not structurally transferable to this neutral polycyclic lactone.",
      "card_ids": ["C09", "C31"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "current_gold_voting_records",
